; host/aot_cache.bl — the pinned HOST MODULE for `Elixir.BeamLisp.AOTCache`.
;
; This file is not a namespace. It is a `.bl` SOURCE that the bootstrap seed
; compiles with `BeamLisp.AOT/compile-host-file` into ONE exact-named beam
; (`Elixir.BeamLisp.AOTCache.beam`) whose top-level `defn`s are plain exported
; functions — the exact call surface every caller already names at
; `Elixir.BeamLisp.AOTCache`, so no caller is renamed. The pinned beam is
; committed into the floor (`priv/bootstrap/seed/`) and installed by
; `Bootstrap.install!/1`; `lib/beam_lisp/aot_cache.ex` is retained until the
; seed carries this beam, then recalled.
;
; WHY A PINNED MODULE AND NOT A NAMESPACE. `AOTCache` is asked for the
; TOOLCHAIN KEY before the language exists. `bin/bl`'s boot program calls
; `BeamLisp.AOTCache.current_compiler_key/0` to judge whether the boot tier in
; `build/` is this tree's generation, and `Bootstrap.install!/1` (in the
; rebuild child) calls `compiler_key/0` and `build_key/0` to judge the floor —
; both BEFORE `ensure_all_started`/`BeamLisp.init`, so before a single
; `BeamLisp.Ns.*` beam is interned. A module on that path can never itself be
; an AOT-rebuilt `BeamLisp.Ns.*` namespace (the bootstrap circle again), so it
; is a pinned host beam instead.
;
; ── THE PREBOOT CONSTRAINT: NO Rt, NO core ──────────────────────────────────
;
; The pinned beam must RUN with nothing on the code path but Elixir/OTP, the
; pinned `Elixir.BeamLisp.Tiers` leaf it asks where the sources are, and itself.
; That is stronger than "does not call the shim": every BL convenience that
; compiles to a call into the runtime is forbidden, because `BeamLisp.Ns.Rt`
; and `BeamLisp.Env` are not loaded at preboot and `core`'s vars are not
; interned. The compiler lowers a bare `(list …)` to `BeamLisp.Ns.Core.list__bl_v`
; and a keyword/`str`/`nil?`/`case`/map-literal to a `BeamLisp.Ns.Rt` or
; `BeamLisp.Env` call — all of which are `undef` before the floor boots. So this
; file is written in the surface the BEAM itself provides:
;
;   * `erlang/*` BIFs — `setelement`, `make_tuple`, `tuple_to_list`, `element`,
;     `is_*`, `==`, `+`, `-`, `>`, `apply`, … — are remote calls to `:erlang`,
;     free of any runtime;
;   * `lst`/`tup`/`bcat` build a list, a tuple and a binary from BIFs alone
;     (`xs` as a rest argument IS a list; `list_to_tuple`/`list_to_binary` do
;     the rest), which is why they exist instead of `(list …)`, `{…}` and `str`;
;   * `Enum`, `Map`, `MapSet`, `Keyword`, `Path`, `File`, `System`, `String`,
;     `Regex`, `Base`, `IO`, `Code`, `Module`, `Macro` are host modules:
;     Elixir/OTP, on the path in any `elixir` VM, and the same modules the
;     Elixir twin called. `Enum` invokes the BL closures below as plain funs,
;     exactly as it invoked the Elixir captures it replaces;
;   * `cond`/`if`/`when`/`and`/`or`/`->`/`when-let`/`if-let` are MACROS — they
;     expand at compile time into `if`/`let`, which emit nothing at runtime;
;   * `case`, `(list …)`, `str`, `nil?`, `{}` map literals, vector literals,
;    destructuring, `for`/`doseq` and calling a locally-bound fn are all
;     AVOIDED: each emits a `BeamLisp.Ns.Core`/`Ns.Rt`/`Env`/`Vector` reference
;     (measured per-construct against the emitted atom table), which is exactly
;     the preboot dependency this file must not have. Matching is spelled with
;     `cond` on `erlang/element`/`erlang/tuple_size`; a name a caller must have
;     is spelled with `erlang/atom_to_binary` or `Atom/to_string`.
;
; `test/bl/aot_cache_host_test.bl` proves this twice: it diffs a fresh compile
; of this source against the live Elixir module over a corpus AND over the
; toolchain key, and it runs the emitted beam in a fresh `elixir` child whose
; ONLY added code path entry is that beam (with the pinned `Tiers` beside it) —
; asserting `BeamLisp.Ns.Rt` and `BeamLisp.Ns.Core` are not loaded before,
; during, or after the calls.
;
; ── ABI PARITY IS THE CONTRACT ──────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; Every public function below reproduces its Elixir counterpart clause for
; clause: the same traversal, the same evaluation order, the same return types
; (`{:ok, modules} | :miss`, `{:ok, deleted} | {:error, reason}`), and the same
; ARITY DEFAULTS (`root \\ priv_root()` and `opts \\ []` become explicit
; zero/one-arity clauses that delegate). The compiler key is preserved to the
; BYTE: the same `["elixir:…", "otp:…", "aot_backend:…"] ++ codegen ++
; toolchain_sources` parts, the same NUL-joined sha256, the same source paths
; (`@codegen_modules` order, `priv/host/<leaf>.bl` for the pinned leaves), the
; same `priv/codegen.sources` baking, and the same cache layout
; (`<dir>/<compiler-key>/<closure-key>/{manifest.term,*.beam}` with the v2
; manifest). `AOTCache` is deliberately NOT a member of its own
; `codegen_modules` list — the key cannot hash the module that computes it —
; so this port changes no key.
;
; The exports are the recalled PUBLIC surface plus the private helpers, which
; the pinned emitter also exports because it exports every top-level `defn` it
; compiles (`defn-` included). That is the ONE divergence every pinned port in
; `priv/host/` carries (`compiler_data.bl` ships `invoke1`,
; `proper-listing`, `invalid-input!` the same way). The helper names are the
; recalled private names, so the divergence is exactly "these are now call
; surface too", nothing more. The test pins the export set so a future edit
; cannot widen it silently.
;
; ── TWO DELIBERATE DIVERGENCES IN THE PLUMBING ──────────────────────────────
;
; 1. `codegen_source_roots/0` cannot use `__DIR__`: the recalled `aot_cache.ex`
;    resolves its first root from a COMPILE-TIME absolute path baked into the
;    Elixir beam, and a `.bl` file has no such macro. The first root here is the
;    checkout's `lib/` anchored on `BL_ROOT` (the variable the launcher exports
;    for exactly this class of question) with the process working directory as
;    the fallback — the same rule the pinned `Tiers` leaf's `priv_root` fallback
;    and `priv/build/*.bl` already carry, and the same ANSWER in every real
;    caller: the launcher and the preboot bootstrap both run against the tree.
;    When neither root resolves (a drop, or a run from an unrelated cwd) the live
;    digest answers `:error` and `codegen_part/0` falls to the baked digest —
;    which a checkout writes on every key computation, so the key is still the
;    tree's. The second root (beside `Tiers.priv_root/0`) is identical to the
;    recalled module's, and the code path a release or a running app takes is
;    unchanged.
; 2. A `rescue` becomes an UNTYPED `catch`: the recalled clauses degrade a cache
;    error to `:miss`/`:ok`, and catching a `throw`/`exit` as well only widens
;    the degrade, never changes an answer on a successful path. The pinned
;    compiler's typed catches test `is_struct(e, Mod)`, so spelling every
;    Elixir exception class would add coverage without adding soundness.

(ns host.aot-cache)

; ── the preboot constructors (BIFs alone; see the header) ───────────────────

(defn- lst
  "A plain list of the arguments. A rest argument IS a list, so this compiles to
   argument collection and nothing else — no `BeamLisp.Ns.Core` reference, which
   is what a bare `(list …)` would emit."
  [& xs] xs)

(defn- tup
  "A tuple of the arguments, built the way Erlang builds one."
  [& xs] (erlang/list_to_tuple xs))

(defn- bcat
  "A binary from the arguments (an iolist). Stands in for `str`/`Kernel.<>`,
   both of which compile to a runtime call."
  [& xs] (erlang/list_to_binary xs))

(defn- self_mod
  "The atom THIS source was compiled into, read from a fun literal compiled
   into this file — module-exact, so the same source serves the production atom
   in the seed and a probe atom under test without naming either. The memo keys
   below ride on it."
  [] (erlang/element 2 (erlang/fun_info (fn [] nil) :module)))

; ── the memo keys (the recalled `@toolchain_key_pt` / `@build_key_pt` /
;    `@gc_last_sweep_pt`) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn- toolchain_key_pt [] (tup (self_mod) :toolchain_key))
(defn- build_key_pt [] (tup (self_mod) :build_key))
(defn- gc_last_sweep_pt [] (tup (self_mod) :gc_last_sweep))

; ── the hashed toolchain inventory (the recalled `@codegen_modules` /
;    `@pinned_host_sources`) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; `@codegen_modules` in order. A pinned host leaf whose source moved to
; `priv/host/<leaf>.bl` is named by `pinned_host_source/1`; every other member
; is still authored under `lib/`. `AOTCache` is DELIBERATELY absent: the key
; cannot hash the module that computes it.

(defn- codegen_modules
  "The host modules whose SOURCES can change EMITTED code, in hash order. A
   change to any of them rotates `compiler_key/0` (invalidate every AOT beam).
   `BeamLisp.Compiler` is deliberately absent — since the genesis cutover it is
   a thin facade over the self-hosted `BeamLisp.Ns.Compiler`, whose source is a
   tier-1 toolchain input (`priv/boot/compiler.bl`)."
  []
  '(:Elixir.BeamLisp.AOT
    :Elixir.BeamLisp.AtomGuard
    :Elixir.BeamLisp.CompilerData
    :Elixir.BeamLisp.SourceGraph
    :Elixir.BeamLisp.NamespaceInterface
    :Elixir.BeamLisp.BuildPlan
    :Elixir.BeamLisp.Record
    :Elixir.BeamLisp.Emit
    :Elixir.BeamLisp.Optimize
    :Elixir.BeamLisp.Link
    :Elixir.BeamLisp.Tiers))

(defn- pinned_host_source
  "The `priv/host/<leaf>.bl` a codegen module's exact-name beam is compiled
   from, or nil for an unpinned module. This is the
   one place that names each pinned leaf; without a row the live digest would
   halt on the deleted `.ex` and `codegen_part/0` would silently freeze the key
   on the baked digest (BUG-106). Every migration of a codegen leaf INTO
   `priv/host/` must add its row here."
  [mod]
  (cond
    (erlang/== mod :Elixir.BeamLisp.AOT) "aot.bl"
    (erlang/== mod :Elixir.BeamLisp.AtomGuard) "atom_guard.bl"
    (erlang/== mod :Elixir.BeamLisp.CompilerData) "compiler_data.bl"
    (erlang/== mod :Elixir.BeamLisp.SourceGraph) "source_graph.bl"
    (erlang/== mod :Elixir.BeamLisp.NamespaceInterface) "ns_interface.bl"
    (erlang/== mod :Elixir.BeamLisp.BuildPlan) "build_plan.bl"
    (erlang/== mod :Elixir.BeamLisp.Emit) "emit.bl"
    (erlang/== mod :Elixir.BeamLisp.Optimize) "optimize.bl"
    (erlang/== mod :Elixir.BeamLisp.Link) "link.bl"
    (erlang/== mod :Elixir.BeamLisp.Record) "record.bl"
    (erlang/== mod :Elixir.BeamLisp.Tiers) "tiers.bl"
    :else nil))
; AOTCache is NOT in `pinned_host_source/1` or `codegen_modules/0`, because it
; is not a hashed input: the key it computes must not name the file that computes
; it. (`test/bl/codegen_provenance_test.bl` pins that membership in the `.ex`.)

; Cache controls honor the same process-local overlay as ordinary System APIs,
; without importing Env or Core into this standalone preboot host. Compiler
; source identity below remains anchored on the physical checkout's BL_ROOT.
(defn- cache_environment [key]
  (let [overlay (erlang/get :bl-osenv-overlay)]
    (if (and (erlang/is_map overlay) (maps/is_key key overlay))
      (maps/get key overlay)
      (erlang/apply :Elixir.System :get_env (lst key)))))

; ── whether the cache participates ─────────────────────────────────────────

(defn enabled?
  "Whether the cache participates in compilation. Default on."
  []
  (let [v (cache_environment "BEAM_LISP_AOT_CACHE")]
    (erlang/not (Enum/member? (lst "off" "0" "false") v))))

(defn enabled_off_env
  "The environment variable that turns the cache off."
  []
  "BEAM_LISP_AOT_CACHE")

(defn dir
  "Root of the cache: `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/beam_lisp/aot` or the override.

   Two kinds of entry live under it, and only the first is a GENERATION:

     * `<compiler-key>/<closure-key>/{manifest.term,*.beam}` — one entry per
       (toolchain generation, source closure). `store/4` publishes, `fetch/3`
       links, `cleanup_obsolete_generations/2` sweeps;
     * `repair/…` — the runtime drift gate's scratch space (see
       `BeamLisp.AOT/repair_library/1`): the linked copy of an entry a VM is
       loading, and the throwaway output directory of a compile that is about
       to be published. It is NOT a generation, so the sweeper ignores it;
       only the runtime gate writes there, and it reuses one link directory per
       (generation, namespace)."
  []
  (let [d (cache_environment "BEAM_LISP_AOT_CACHE_DIR")]
    (cond
      (erlang/== d nil)
      (Path/join
        (erlang/apply :filename :basedir (lst :user_cache (erlang/binary_to_list "beam_lisp")))
        "aot")
      :else d)))

(defn aot_backend
  "The body-module backend is `:core`: bl-ANF → Core Erlang → BEAM through the
   boot `lower` namespace. Other settings raise. It lives here, not in
   `BeamLisp.AOT`, because `compiler_key/0` must fold it in — a Core-built beam
   and an Elixir-built beam of the same source are different bytes — and this
   module computes the key before `BeamLisp.AOT` is even a concern."
  []
  (let [b (Application/get_env :beam_lisp :aot_backend :core)]
    (cond
      (erlang/== b :core) :core
      :else
      (erlang/error
        (Elixir.ArgumentError/exception
          (bcat "unsupported AOT backend " (Kernel/inspect b)
                ": the self-hosted compiler emits ANF; use :core"))))))

; ── the tier keys ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn compiler_key
  "Hash of the toolchain that produced a beam. Any change to codegen, the
   toolchain sources, or the Elixir/OTP/backend it runs on yields a new key, so
   stale artifacts compiled by a different toolchain are never linked. Memoized
   in `:persistent_term` (a VM constant in normal use). The app's release
   version is NOT an input: it is metadata, not codegen."
  []
  (let [cached (persistent_term/get (toolchain_key_pt) :undefined)]
    (cond
      (erlang/== cached :undefined)
      (let [k (compute_compiler_key)]
        (persistent_term/put (toolchain_key_pt) k)
        k)
      :else cached)))

(defn current_compiler_key
  "Compute the compiler key WITHOUT the persistent_term memo — the live value
   for the CURRENT toolchain sources on disk. `compiler_key/0` caches its first
   computation for the VM's life; the daemon uses THIS to detect that the
   checkout it serves has drifted from the sources it booted with, which must
   force a restart, not a stale reuse."
  []
  (compute_compiler_key))

(defn current_build_key
  "Like `current_compiler_key/0` for the build tier: the LIVE value, unmemoized."
  []
  (compute_build_key))

(defn build_key
  "Hash of the BUILD DRIVER tier (`priv/build/`). These namespaces decide WHAT
   to build; they cannot change an emitted byte, so their edits must not
   invalidate every beam. The driver's own beams are compiled BY the codegen,
   so this key folds in `compiler_key/0`. Memoized."
  []
  (let [cached (persistent_term/get (build_key_pt) :undefined)]
    (cond
      (erlang/== cached :undefined)
      (let [k (compute_build_key)]
        (persistent_term/put (build_key_pt) k)
        k)
      :else cached)))

(defn- compute_build_key []
  (hash_parts (lists/append (lst (compiler_key)) (build_source_contents))))

(defn- build_source_contents
  "Content of every build-driver source, sorted by path. Read DIRECTLY (no
   reader, no Env) for the same reason `toolchain_source_contents/0` is: this
   runs before `BeamLisp.init/0`. An unreadable file contributes nothing rather
   than crashing the key computation."
  []
  (Enum/flat_map
    (Enum/sort (Path/wildcard (Path/join (BeamLisp.Tiers/build_dir) "**/*.bl")))
    (fn [path]
      (let [r (File/read path)]
        (cond
          (and (erlang/is_tuple r) (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 r)))
          (lst (erlang/element 2 r))
          :else '())))))

(defn key_for_source
  "The key a SOURCE's beam is stamped with: the tier it belongs to. `boot/` and
   every ordinary source use the codegen key; `build/` uses `build_key/0`. The
   build manifest and the emitter both route through here, so a beam's stamp and
   the gate that judges it cannot disagree."
  ([path] (key_for_source path (BeamLisp.Tiers/priv_root)))
  ([path root]
   (cond
     (BeamLisp.Tiers/build_source? path root) (build_key)
     :else (compiler_key))))

(defn key_for_ns
  "The key a NAMESPACE's beam is stamped with: `BeamLisp.Tiers.tier_of_ns/1`."
  [ns]
  (key_for_tier (BeamLisp.Tiers/tier_of_ns ns)))

(defn key_for_tier
  "The key for a tier: `:build` → `build_key/0`, anything else → `compiler_key/0`."
  [tier]
  (cond
    (erlang/== tier :build) (build_key)
    :else (compiler_key)))

(defn reset_compiler_key
  "Drop the memoized toolchain key so the next `compiler_key/0` recomputes it.
   The key is a VM-constant in normal use, so this exists only for tests that
   mutate a hashed input in-process and must observe the new key."
  []
  (persistent_term/erase (toolchain_key_pt)))

(defn reset_keys
  "Drop BOTH memoized tier keys, so the next `compiler_key/0` and `build_key/0`
   recompute. Tests that mutate a hashed input in-process use this."
  []
  (persistent_term/erase (toolchain_key_pt))
  (persistent_term/erase (build_key_pt))
  :ok)

; ── the toolchain key computation ──────────────────────────────────────────

(defn- compute_compiler_key
  "The key: the runtime triple, the codegen contribution and the tier-1 sources,
   NUL-joined and hashed. The app `:vsn` is DELIBERATELY NOT hashed — it is
   release METADATA, not a codegen input, and keying the generation on it
   manufactures a generation change out of a release stamp."
  []
  (let [parts (lst (bcat "elixir:" (System/version))
                   (bcat "otp:" (erlang/list_to_binary (erlang/system_info :otp_release)))
                   (bcat "aot_backend:" (erlang/atom_to_binary (aot_backend) :utf8)))
        codegen (codegen_part)
        toolchain_sources (toolchain_source_contents)]
    (hash_parts (lists/append parts (lists/append codegen toolchain_sources)))))

(defn- codegen_part
  "The codegen host's contribution to the toolchain key, as a list of parts.

   Three images, three answers: LIVE sources present → hash them and BAKE the
   digest for images that ship none; a baked digest present → a release drop,
   whose packing checkout wrote the only compiler-independent answer; neither →
   beam BYTES, the pre-BUG-048 rule, kept so drops built before
   `priv/codegen.sources` existed compute the key their beams were stamped
   with."
  []
  (let [live (live_codegen_digest)]
    (cond
      (erlang/not (erlang/== live nil))
      (do
        (bake_codegen_digest live)
        (lst (bcat "codegen-source:" live)))
      :else
      (let [baked (baked_codegen_digest)]
        (cond
          (erlang/not (erlang/== baked nil))
          (lst (bcat "codegen-source:" baked))
          :else (legacy_codegen_beam_bytes))))))

(defn- live_codegen_digest
  "sha256 over the codegen modules' SOURCE files, each named by its module so a
   rename or a reordering cannot collide. nil when ANY source is missing: a
   partial answer would describe a different toolchain than the one running.

   SOURCES, NOT BEAMS (BUG-048): beam bytes are written by two compilers in the
   same tree, so a key over them is a property of the compiler that LAST WROTE
   the beams rather than of the toolchain. A source digest is
   compiler-independent, which is what a toolchain key has always claimed."
  []
  (let [parts (Enum/reduce_while (codegen_modules) '()
                (fn [mod acc]
                  (let [r (File/read (codegen_source_path mod))]
                    (cond
                      (and (erlang/is_tuple r) (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 r)))
                      (tup :cont (lists/append (lst (erlang/atom_to_binary mod :utf8)
                                                     (erlang/element 2 r))
                                                acc))
                      :else (tup :halt :missing)))))]
    (cond
      (erlang/== parts :missing) nil
      :else (hash_parts (lists/append (lst "codegen") (Enum/reverse parts))))))

(defn- codegen_source_path
  "The source path for a codegen module: the pinned `.bl` for a leaf in
   `pinned_host_source/1`, else `lib/beam_lisp/<name>.ex` — derived from the
   module name rather than listed beside it, so a module added to
   `codegen_modules/0` cannot be silently uncovered."
  [mod]
  (let [leaf (pinned_host_source mod)]
    (cond
      (erlang/not (erlang/== leaf nil))
      (let [relative (bcat "../priv/host/" leaf)
            found (Enum/find_value (codegen_source_roots)
                    (fn [root]
                      (let [path (Path/expand relative root)]
                        (if (File/exists? path) path))))]
        (cond
          (erlang/== found nil) (Path/expand relative (erlang/hd (codegen_source_roots)))
          :else found))
      :else
      (let [name (bcat (Enum/map_join (Module/split mod) "/" (fn [s] (Macro/underscore s))) ".ex")
            found (Enum/find_value (codegen_source_roots)
                    (fn [root]
                      (let [path (Path/join root name)]
                        (if (File/exists? path) path))))]
        (cond
          (erlang/== found nil) (Path/join (erlang/hd (codegen_source_roots)) name)
          :else found)))))

(defn- codegen_source_roots
  "Where the codegen sources live, in order of authority: the checkout's `lib/`
   (anchored on `BL_ROOT`, which the launcher exports, and falling back to the
   process working directory — a `.bl` source has no `__DIR__`; see the header),
   then `lib/` beside the app's `priv/`. The `.ex` modules and the pinned
   `priv/host/*.bl` leaves are resolved beside these. A root that does not exist
   simply loses the `File.exists?` race and the next is tried."
  []
  (let [anchor (let [r (erlang/apply :Elixir.System :get_env (lst "BL_ROOT"))]
                 (cond (erlang/== r nil) (System/cwd) :else r))]
    (lst (Path/expand (Path/join anchor "lib"))
         (Path/join (Path/dirname (BeamLisp.Tiers/priv_root)) "lib"))))

(defn- baked_codegen_sources_path
  "Where the digest is baked, for images that ship no source. Beside the tiers in
   `priv/` because assembling a drop copies `priv/` wholesale."
  []
  (Path/join (BeamLisp.Tiers/priv_root) "codegen.sources"))

(defn- baked_codegen_digest
  "The baked digest as a 64-hex binary, or nil when the file is absent,
   malformed, or unreadable."
  []
  (try
    (let [r (File/read (baked_codegen_sources_path))]
      (cond
        (and (erlang/is_tuple r) (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 r)))
        (let [d (List/first (String/split (erlang/element 2 r) "\n"))]
          (cond
            (erlang/is_binary d)
            (cond
              (Regex/match? (Regex/compile! "\\A[0-9a-f]{64}\\z") d) d
              :else nil)
            :else nil))
        :else nil))
    (catch _e nil)))

(defn- temp_path
  "A cache staging path must be unique across independent OS VMs, not only
   Erlang processes in one VM. Keep this helper usable before core loads."
  [path]
  (bcat path ".tmp-" (os/getpid) "-"
        (erlang/integer_to_list (System/unique_integer (lst :positive)))))

(defn- bake_codegen_digest
  "Best-effort and atomic: write the digest for images that ship no source. This
   runs inside key computation, reached from boot paths that must never fail on
   a cache, so a read-only image ignores the failure."
  [digest]
  (try
    (let [path (baked_codegen_sources_path)
          r (File/read path)
          current (cond
                    (and (erlang/is_tuple r) (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 r)))
                    (String/trim (erlang/element 2 r))
                    :else nil)]
      (cond
        (erlang/not (erlang/== current digest))
        (let [tmp (temp_path path)]
          (File/write! tmp (bcat digest "\n"))
          (File/rename! tmp path))
        :else :ok))
    :ok
    (catch _e :ok)))

(defn- legacy_codegen_beam_bytes
  "The pre-BUG-048 rule, kept verbatim for images built under it.
   `:code.get_object_code/1` answers the module's bytes wherever the code server
   found them — a real ebin OR an escript archive, where reading `:code.which/1`
   with `File.read` fails. Degrade (never crash) when a module is absent."
  []
  (Enum/flat_map (codegen_modules)
    (fn [mod]
      (let [r (code/get_object_code mod)]
        (cond
          (and (erlang/is_tuple r)
               (erlang/== 3 (erlang/tuple_size r))
               (erlang/== mod (erlang/element 1 r)))
          (lst (erlang/element 2 r))
          :else '())))))

(defn- toolchain_source_contents
  "Content of every tier-1 source: everything under `priv/boot/` — the
   self-hosted compiler, the reader providers, the ambient prelude — plus the
   `priv/self/` oracle while the `:core` backend still serves it, sorted by path
   for determinism. The boot tier is closed under `:require`, so hashing the
   DIRECTORY is the closure — no header parse, no reader, nothing this runs
   before. Resolved by DIRECT file reads: this runs from `Bootstrap.install!/1`
   BEFORE `BeamLisp.init/0`."
  []
  (let [boot (Path/wildcard (Path/join (BeamLisp.Tiers/boot_dir) "**/*.bl"))
        oracles (cond
                  (erlang/== (aot_backend) :core)
                  (Path/wildcard (Path/join (BeamLisp.Tiers/priv_root) "self/**/*.bl"))
                  :else '())]
    (Enum/map (Enum/sort (lists/append boot oracles)) (fn [p] (File/read! p)))))

; ── the closure key ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn closure_key
  "Hash of one source's closure: its absolute path + content hash and those of
   every transitive `:require` target within the build's source set. `deps` maps
   source path → required source paths; `hashes` maps source path → content
   hash. Requires outside the source set (the core prelude) are covered by
   `compiler_key/0`."
  [path deps hashes]
  (let [closure (Enum/sort (closure_walk path deps (MapSet/new)))
        entries (Enum/map closure (fn [p] (bcat p ":" (Map/fetch! hashes p))))]
    (hash_parts entries)))

(defn- closure_walk
  "Every source reachable from `path` through `deps`, `seen` a `MapSet` of
   already-visited paths (so a cycle terminates)."
  [path deps seen]
  (cond
    (MapSet/member? seen path) seen
    :else
    (Enum/reduce (Map/get deps path '()) (MapSet/put seen path)
      (fn [dep acc] (closure_walk dep deps acc)))))

; ── the cache entry: fetch, store, validate ────────────────────────────────

(defn fetch
  "Link a cached entry's beams into `compile_path`. Returns `{:ok, modules}`
   when the entry existed and every beam materialised, `:miss` otherwise (absent
   entry, or any link/copy failure — the caller compiles instead). The four-arg
   form separates a context-specific cache address from actual source provenance."
  ([compiler_key closure_key compile_path]
   (fetch compiler_key closure_key compile_path closure_key))
  ([compiler_key cache_key compile_path source_key]
  (let [entry (entry_dir compiler_key cache_key)
        modules (valid_keyed_entry entry compiler_key source_key)]
    (cond
      (erlang/== modules nil) :miss
      :else
      (cond
        (erlang/== :ok (link_beams entry compile_path modules)) (tup :ok modules)
        :else :miss)))))

(defn store
  "Publish the beams for `modules` (already in `compile_path`) under the given
   keys. Atomic via temp-dir + rename; failures are ignored. The manifest is
   `%{version: 2, modules: modules, digests: digests}` — the SAME layout the
   recalled module wrote, so entries are interchangeable in both directions.
   The five-arg form validates source_key while publishing under cache_key."
  ([compiler_key closure_key compile_path modules]
   (store compiler_key closure_key compile_path modules closure_key))
  ([compiler_key cache_key compile_path modules source_key]
  (let [final (entry_dir compiler_key cache_key)
        tmp (temp_path final)]
    (try
      (do
        (File/mkdir_p! tmp)
        (Enum/each modules
          (fn [mod]
            (File/cp! (Path/join compile_path (beam_file mod))
                      (Path/join tmp (beam_file mod)))))
        (let [digests (Map/new
                        (Enum/map modules
                          (fn [mod]
                            (tup mod (crypto/hash :sha256
                                       (File/read! (Path/join tmp (beam_file mod))))))))]
          (File/write! (Path/join tmp "manifest.term")
                       (erlang/term_to_binary
                         (Map/put (Map/put (Map/put (Map/new) :version 2)
                                           :modules modules)
                                  :digests digests))))
        (cond
          (erlang/== nil (valid_keyed_entry tmp compiler_key source_key)) (File/rm_rf! tmp)
          :else
          (global/trans (tup (tup (toolchain_key_pt) :publish final) (erlang/self))
          (fn []
            (cond
              (erlang/not (erlang/== nil (valid_keyed_entry final compiler_key source_key))) (File/rm_rf! tmp)
              :else (do (File/rm_rf! final) (File/rename! tmp final))))
          (lst (erlang/node))))
        (maybe_cleanup_obsolete_generations compiler_key)
        :ok)
      (catch _e (do (File/rm_rf tmp) :ok))))))

(defn- valid_entry
  "The module list of a COMPLETE entry, or nil. A manifest is trusted only when
   it is the v2 shape and every beam it names still hashes to its recorded
   digest: the entry is on-disk input, never assumed."
  [entry]
  (try
    (let [r (File/read (Path/join entry "manifest.term"))]
      (cond
        (erlang/not (and (erlang/is_tuple r) (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 r)))) nil
        :else
        (let [term (safe_term (erlang/element 2 r))]
          (cond
            (erlang/not (erlang/is_map term)) nil
            (erlang/not (erlang/== 2 (Map/get term :version))) nil
            :else
            (let [modules (Map/get term :modules)
                  digests (Map/get term :digests)]
              (cond
                (erlang/not (erlang/is_list modules)) nil
                (Enum/all? modules (fn [mod] (valid_beam? entry digests mod))) modules
                :else nil))))))
    (catch _e nil)))

(defn beam_provenance_matches?
  "Read provenance without loading or initializing code. Build receipts and
   cache digests do not prove that a namespace beam belongs to their key."
  [path compiler_key closure_key]
  (try
    (let [r (beam_lib/chunks (String/to_charlist path) (lst :attributes))]
      (cond
        (erlang/not (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 r))) false
        :else
        (let [chunks (erlang/element 2 (erlang/element 2 r))
              attrs (Keyword/get chunks :attributes)]
          (provenance_attributes_match? attrs compiler_key closure_key))))
    (catch _e false)))

(defn- provenance_attributes_match?
  [attrs compiler_key closure_key]
  ; BL's Erlang descriptor persists a binary; Elixir's registered attribute
  ; persists a singleton list. Both encode the same exact key, not a wildcard.
  (let [source (Keyword/get attrs :bl_source_hash)
        compiler (Keyword/get attrs :bl_compiler_key)
        ;; Source keys alone cannot identify the executing pinned emitter:
        ;; an old host can stamp its old output with newly edited sources.
        replay (Keyword/get attrs :bl_aot_replay_version)]
    (and (or (erlang/== source closure_key) (erlang/== source (lst closure_key)))
         (or (erlang/== compiler compiler_key) (erlang/== compiler (lst compiler_key))
             ;; A FLOOR (boot/build tier) beam carries no key in its bytes; the
             ;; cache entry's address and the floor claim name its generation.
             (and (nil? compiler) (floor_unit? attrs)))
         (or (erlang/== replay 1) (erlang/== replay (lst 1))))))

(defn- floor_unit? [attrs]
  (let [raw (Keyword/get attrs :bl_unit_namespace)
        ns (if (and (erlang/is_list raw) (erlang/== 1 (erlang/length raw))) (erlang/hd raw) raw)]
    (and (erlang/is_binary ns)
         (let [tier (BeamLisp.Tiers/tier_of_ns ns)]
           (or (erlang/== tier :boot) (erlang/== tier :build))))))

(defn- cached_module_matches?
  [entry mod compiler_key closure_key]
  (cond
    ; Native and generic cache clients retain their digest-only contract.
    (erlang/not (String/starts_with? (Atom/to_string mod) "Elixir.BeamLisp.Ns.")) true
    :else
    (try
      (let [path (Path/join entry (beam_file mod))
            r (beam_lib/chunks (String/to_charlist path) (lst :exports :attributes))]
        (cond
          (erlang/not (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 r))) false
          :else
          (let [chunks (erlang/element 2 (erlang/element 2 r))
                exports (Keyword/get chunks :exports)]
            (cond
              (Enum/member? exports (tup :__bl_ns_defs__ 0))
              (provenance_attributes_match? (Keyword/get chunks :attributes) compiler_key closure_key)
              :else true))))
      (catch _e false))))

(defn- valid_keyed_entry
  [entry compiler_key closure_key]
  (let [modules (valid_entry entry)]
    (cond
      (erlang/== nil modules) nil
      (Enum/all? modules
        (fn [mod] (cached_module_matches? entry mod compiler_key closure_key))) modules
      :else nil)))

(defn- valid_beam?
  "Whether `mod`'s beam in `entry` still hashes to the digest the manifest
   records for it."
  [entry digests mod]
  (let [r (File/read (Path/join entry (beam_file mod)))]
    (cond
      (and (erlang/is_tuple r) (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 r)))
      (erlang/== (crypto/hash :sha256 (erlang/element 2 r)) (Map/get digests mod))
      :else false)))

(defn- safe_term
  "The decoded manifest when it is a map carrying a list `:modules`, else nil. A
   malformed entry degrades to a miss."
  [bin]
  (try
    (let [t (erlang/binary_to_term bin)]
      (cond
        (and (erlang/is_map t) (erlang/is_list (Map/get t :modules))) t
        :else nil))
    (catch _e nil)))

; ── generation cleanup ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn cleanup_obsolete_generations
  "Remove obsolete compiler-key generations from the configured cache root. The
   active generation is always retained. Only real directories whose names are
   lowercase sha256 keys are candidates; symlinks and all other entries are
   ignored. Cleanup is bounded by `:max_delete` per call and is best-effort.
   Retention defaults can be overridden with `config :beam_lisp,
   :aot_cache_gc, keep_generations: 8, max_age_days: 30, max_delete: 4,
   interval_ms: 3_600_000`; explicit options override config."
  ([active_key] (cleanup_obsolete_generations active_key '()))
  ([active_key opts] :when (string? active_key)
   (try
     (let [options (gc_options opts)
           root (dir)
           listed (File/ls root)]
       (cond
         (erlang/not (and (erlang/is_tuple listed) (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 listed))))
         (cond
           (and (erlang/is_tuple listed)
                (erlang/== 2 (erlang/tuple_size listed))
                (erlang/== :enoent (erlang/element 2 listed)))
           (tup :ok '())
           :else (tup :error (erlang/element 2 listed)))
         :else
         (let [entries (erlang/element 2 listed)
               generations (Enum/sort_by
                             (Enum/flat_map
                               (Enum/reject
                                 (Enum/filter entries (fn [n] (valid_compiler_key? n)))
                                 (fn [n] (erlang/== n active_key)))
                               (fn [n] (generation_info root n)))
                             (fn [g] (Map/get g :mtime))
                             :desc)
               now (System/os_time :second)
               keep (erlang/max (erlang/- (Keyword/get options :keep_generations) 1) 0)
               age_limit (erlang/* (Keyword/get options :max_age_days) 86400)
               candidates (Enum/take
                            (Enum/sort_by
                              (Enum/map
                                (Enum/filter (Enum/with_index generations)
                                  (fn [gi]
                                    (or (erlang/>= (erlang/element 2 gi) keep)
                                        (erlang/> (erlang/- now (Map/get (erlang/element 1 gi) :mtime))
                                                  age_limit))))
                                (fn [gi] (erlang/element 1 gi)))
                              (fn [g] (Map/get g :mtime)))
                            (Keyword/get options :max_delete))
               deleted (Enum/flat_map candidates
                         (fn [g]
                           (let [rr (File/rm_rf (Map/get g :path))]
                             (cond
                               (and (erlang/is_tuple rr) (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 rr)))
                               (lst (Map/get g :name))
                               :else '()))))]
           (tup :ok deleted))))
     (catch _e (tup :ok '())))))

(defn reset_cleanup_throttle
  "Drop the throttle slot so the next `store/4` sweeps again."
  []
  (persistent_term/erase (gc_last_sweep_pt)))

(defn- maybe_cleanup_obsolete_generations
  "Sweep obsolete generations, at most once per `:interval_ms`, serialized on a
   global lock so parallel build workers share one sweep budget — a cold wave
   cannot multiply `max_delete` by its worker count."
  [active_key]
  (global/trans (tup (gc_last_sweep_pt) (erlang/self))
    (fn []
      (let [options (gc_options '())
            now (System/monotonic_time :millisecond)
            root (dir)
            last (persistent_term/get (gc_last_sweep_pt) nil)
            due (cond
                  (and (erlang/is_tuple last)
                       (erlang/== 2 (erlang/tuple_size last))
                       (erlang/== root (erlang/element 1 last)))
                  (erlang/>= (erlang/- now (erlang/element 2 last))
                             (Keyword/get options :interval_ms))
                  :else true)]
        (cond
          due (do
                (persistent_term/put (gc_last_sweep_pt) (tup root now))
                (cleanup_obsolete_generations active_key options))
          :else :ok))))
  :ok)

(defn- gc_options
  "The merge of `@gc_defaults`, the application's `:aot_cache_gc` config and the
   explicit overrides, with every value coerced to its positive/non-negative
   integer shape."
  [overrides]
  (let [configured (Application/get_env :beam_lisp :aot_cache_gc '())
        defaults (gc_defaults)
        merged (Keyword/merge
                 (Keyword/merge defaults (cond (Keyword/keyword? configured) configured :else '()))
                 overrides)]
    (lst (tup :keep_generations
              (positive_integer (Keyword/get merged :keep_generations)
                                (Keyword/get defaults :keep_generations)))
         (tup :max_age_days
              (positive_integer (Keyword/get merged :max_age_days)
                                (Keyword/get defaults :max_age_days)))
         (tup :max_delete
              (positive_integer (Keyword/get merged :max_delete)
                                (Keyword/get defaults :max_delete)))
         (tup :interval_ms
              (non_negative_integer (Keyword/get merged :interval_ms)
                                    (Keyword/get defaults :interval_ms))))))

(defn- gc_defaults
  "`keep_generations: 8, max_age_days: 30, max_delete: 4, interval_ms: 3_600_000`."
  []
  (lst (tup :keep_generations 8)
       (tup :max_age_days 30)
       (tup :max_delete 4)
       (tup :interval_ms 3600000)))

(defn- positive_integer
  "`value` when it is an integer > 0, else `default`."
  [value default]
  (cond
    (and (erlang/is_integer value) (erlang/> value 0)) value
    :else default))

(defn- non_negative_integer
  "`value` when it is an integer >= 0, else `default`."
  [value default]
  (cond
    (and (erlang/is_integer value) (erlang/>= value 0)) value
    :else default))

(defn- valid_compiler_key?
  "Whether `name` is a lowercase sha256 key — the only directory names cleanup
   will consider."
  [name]
  (Regex/match? (Regex/compile! "\\A[0-9a-f]{64}\\z") name))

(defn- generation_info
  "A `[%{name: …, path: …, mtime: …}]` for `name` under `root` when it is a real
   directory (mtime in POSIX seconds), else `[]`. Symlinks are deliberately not
   directories here: `File.stat`-free `lstat` reports the LINK's type."
  [root name]
  (let [path (Path/join root name)
        r (File/lstat path (lst (tup :time :posix)))]
    (cond
      (and (erlang/is_tuple r) (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 r)))
      (let [st (erlang/element 2 r)]
        (cond
          (erlang/== :directory (Map/get st :type))
          (lst (Map/put (Map/put (Map/put (Map/new) :name name) :path path)
                        :mtime (Map/get st :mtime)))
          :else '()))
      :else '())))

; ── internals ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(defn run_init_modules
  "Replay a fetched unit once per environment and exact artifact. Physical code
   publication uses native lease/soft-purge fences. Reentrant or partially failed
   initialization refuses; a fresh environment is the retry boundary."
  [modules compile_path]
  (BeamLisp.Loader/assert_initializer_execution_allowed! :aot-cache-replay)
  (let [ordered (Enum/sort modules) key (tup :aot_replay ordered)
        fingerprint (Enum/map ordered (fn [mod]
          (let [path (Path/join compile_path (beam_file mod)) read (File/read path)]
            (if (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 read))
              (tup mod (crypto/hash :sha256 (erlang/element 2 read)))
              (tup mod (erlang/apply mod :module_info (lst :md5)))))))
        identity (fn [] (Enum/map ordered (fn [mod]
                         (tup mod (erlang/apply mod :module_info (lst :md5))))))]
    (BeamLisp.Env/with_namespace_lock (tup :aot_replay (tup (BeamLisp.Env/env_id) ordered))
      (fn []
        (let [found (BeamLisp.Env/lookup_own key)
              previous (if (erlang/== :error found) nil (erlang/element 2 found))]
          (cond
            (and previous (erlang/== :ready (Map/get previous :status))
                 (erlang/== fingerprint (Map/get previous :fingerprint))
                 (erlang/== (identity) (Map/get previous :installed))) :ok
            (and previous (erlang/not (erlang/== :ready (Map/get previous :status))))
            (erlang/error (tup :aot_replay_incomplete ordered))
            :else
            (do
              (BeamLisp.Env/put_key key (Map/new (lst (tup :status :initializing))))
              (try
                (Enum/each modules (fn [mod] (ensure_module_loaded mod compile_path)))
                (Enum/each
                  (Enum/filter modules (fn [mod] (erlang/function_exported mod :__bl_init__ 0)))
                  (fn [mod] (erlang/apply mod :__bl_init__ '())))
                (BeamLisp.Env/put_key key (Map/new (lst (tup :status :ready)
                   (tup :fingerprint fingerprint) (tup :installed (identity)))))
                :ok
                (catch error
                  (BeamLisp.Env/put_key key (Map/new (lst (tup :status :failed))))
                  (erlang/error error))))))))))

(defn- ensure_module_loaded
  "Publish the artifact's exact bytes through native physical ownership fences.
   A loaded same-named module is not proof it matches this cache entry."
  [mod compile_path]
  (let [beam (Path/join compile_path (beam_file mod)) read (File/read beam)]
    (if (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 read))
      (do (BeamLisp.Env/publish_binaries! (lst (tup mod (erlang/element 2 read))) beam)
          (tup :module mod))
      (if (erlang/module_loaded mod) (tup :module mod)
        (erlang/error (tup :missing_aot_replay_module mod))))))

(defn- entry_dir
  "The directory an entry lives in: `<dir>/<compiler-key>/<closure-key>`, with
   both keys refused unless they are safe path components and the generation
   refused if it is a symlink."
  [compiler_key closure_key]
  (let [keys (lst compiler_key closure_key)
        safe? (Regex/compile! "\\A[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\z")]
    (cond
      (erlang/not (and (Enum/all? keys (fn [k] (erlang/is_binary k)))
                       (Enum/all? keys (fn [k] (and (erlang/is_binary k)
                                                    (Regex/match? safe? k))))))
      (erlang/error (Elixir.ArgumentError/exception "cache keys must be safe path components"))
      :else
      (let [generation (Path/join (dir) compiler_key)
            r (File/lstat generation)]
        (cond
          (and (erlang/is_tuple r)
               (erlang/== :ok (erlang/element 1 r))
               (erlang/== :symlink (Map/get (erlang/element 2 r) :type)))
          (erlang/error (Elixir.ArgumentError/exception "cache generation cannot be a symlink"))
          :else (Path/join generation closure_key))))))

(defn- beam_file
  "The beam filename for a module atom."
  [mod]
  (bcat (erlang/atom_to_binary mod :utf8) ".beam"))

(defn- link_beams
  "Materialise into a private temporary name, then atomically replace the
   destination. Concurrent VMs may share compile_path: copying onto another
   VM's hardlink would truncate the immutable cache entry itself."
  [entry compile_path modules]
  (File/mkdir_p! compile_path)
  (Enum/reduce_while modules :ok
    (fn [mod acc]
      (let [src (Path/join entry (beam_file mod))
            dst (Path/join compile_path (beam_file mod))
            tmp (temp_path dst)]
        (cond
          (erlang/not (File/exists? src)) (tup :halt :error)
          :else
          (try
            (let [link (File/ln src tmp)
                  linked (cond
                           (erlang/== :ok link) :ok
                           (erlang/== (tup :error :eexist) link) :error
                           :else (copy src tmp))]
              (if (and (erlang/== :ok linked) (erlang/== :ok (File/rename tmp dst)))
                (tup :cont :ok) (tup :halt :error)))
            (finally (File/rm tmp))))))))

(defn- copy
  "A real copy of `src` to `dst`, `:ok` or `:error`."
  [src dst]
  (cond
    (erlang/== :ok (File/cp src dst)) :ok
    :else :error))

(defn- hash_parts
  "sha256 over the parts joined by a NUL byte, lowercase hex — the one hashing
   rule every key here uses."
  [parts]
  (Base/encode16
    (crypto/hash :sha256 (IO/iodata_to_binary (Enum/intersperse parts 0)))
    (lst (tup :case :lower))))
